```

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');
app.use(helmet());          // defaults to many secure headers

// Optional: Turn on their HTTPS‑only mode (HSTS).
app.use(helmet.hsts({
  maxAge: 31536000,        // 1 year
  includeSubDomains: true,
  preload: true
}));
```

### 3.2 Enforce HTTPS (A3)

In production, terminate TLS at a reverse proxy (NGINX, HAProxy) or use `https` Node API. Add this simple check if you decide to run Node directly:

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (!req.secure) { // req.secure === true when request is HTTPS
    return res.redirect('https://' + req.headers.host + req.url);
  }
  next();
});
```

> **Note**: Running on port 3000 without HTTPS is fine for local dev but must be behind HTTPS in prod.

### 3.3 Enable CORS Policy (A6)

If the API is consumed by browsers, provide a strict CORS policy.

